Theorem (Non-Finite Set of Primes):
The set of prime numbers is not finite, meaning there are infinitely many primes.

theorem primes_infinite: "¬ finite {p. prime p}"
@proof
  @obtain b where "prime b" "Max {p. prime p} < b"
@qed

Theorem (Existence of Larger Primes):
There exists a prime number \(p\) such that \(p\) is greater than any given natural number \(n\).

theorem bigger_prime [resolve]: "∃p. prime p ∧ n < p"
@proof
  @obtain p where "prime p" "p dvd fact n + 1"
  @case "n ≥ p" @with @have "(p::nat) dvd fact n" @end
@qed

