Theorem (Complementary Angles in Geometry):
Given two angles \(A\) and \(A1\) that are supplementary (their sum equals 180 degrees), and points \(B\) and \(B1\) on the lines containing these angles, the theorem states that the angle formed by the intersection of the lines through \(C\) and \(C1\) with the lines through \(B\) and \(B1\) is congruent to the angle formed by the intersection of the lines through \(D\) and \(D1\) with the lines through \(B\) and \(B1\). In other words, \(\angle(C, B, D) \cong \angle(C1, B1, D1)\).

theorem (in Congruence_Rule) Ang_complementary :
  assumes
    "Def (Ang (An A B C))"
    "Def (Ang (An A1 B1 C1))"
    "Cong (Geos (Ang (An A B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An A1 B1 C1)) add Emp)"
    "Bet_Point (Se A D) B"
    "Bet_Point (Se A1 D1) B1"
  shows
    "Cong (Geos (Ang (An C B D)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An C1 B1 D1)) add Emp)"
proof -
  from assms have "∃p. Cong (Geos (Ang (An A B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An p B1 C1)) add Emp)
    ∧ Eq (Geos (Ang (An A1 B1 C1)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An p B1 C1)) add Emp)
    ∧ Eq (Geos (Seg (Se B A)) add Emp) (Geos (Seg (Se B1 p)) add Emp)
    ∧ Line_on (Li B1 A1) p ∧ ¬ Bet_Point (Se p A1) B1 ∧ Def (Ang (An p B1 C1))" by (simp add:Ang_replace)
  then obtain A2 :: Point where P1 : "Cong (Geos (Ang (An A B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An A2 B1 C1)) add Emp) 
    ∧ Eq (Geos (Seg (Se B A)) add Emp) (Geos (Seg (Se B1 A2)) add Emp) ∧ Line_on (Li B1 A1) A2
    ∧ ¬ Bet_Point (Se A2 A1) B1 ∧ Def (Ang (An A2 B1 C1))" by blast
  from assms P1 have "∃p. Cong (Geos (Ang (An A B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An A2 B1 p)) add Emp)
    ∧ Eq (Geos (Ang (An A2 B1 C1)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An A2 B1 p)) add Emp) 
    ∧ Eq (Geos (Seg (Se B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Seg (Se B1 p)) add Emp) 
    ∧ Line_on (Li B1 C1) p ∧ ¬ Bet_Point (Se p C1) B1 ∧ Def (Ang (An A2 B1 p))" by (simp add:Ang_replace)
  then obtain C2 :: Point where P2 : "Cong (Geos (Ang (An A B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Ang (An A2 B1 C2)) add Emp) 
    ∧ Eq (Geos (Seg (Se B C)) add Emp) (Geos (Seg (Se B1 C2)) add Emp) ∧ Line_on (Li B1 C1) C2
    ∧ ¬ Bet_Point (Se C2 C1) B1 ∧ Def (Ang (An A2 B1 C2))" by blast
  from assms have "Def (Tri (Tr A B C))" by (simp add:Ang_to_Tri)
  then have P3 : "Def (Tri (Tr B A C))" by (blast intro:Tri_def_rev Tri_def_trans)
  from P2 have "Def (Tri (Tr A2 B1 C2))" by (simp add:Ang_to_Tri)
  then have P4 : "Def (Tri (Tr B1 A2 C2))" by (blast intro:Tri_def_rev Tri_def_trans)
